1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,711
Crap! There's a frog doing the right crawl!

2
00:01:53,711 --> 00:01:55,411
Come on! After him!

3
00:01:55,411 --> 00:01:56,411
Aye-aye!

4
00:01:59,311 --> 00:02:02,211
Now, what is a lighthouse doing way out here?

5
00:02:02,211 --> 00:02:04,011
I wonder if anyone lives there?

6
00:02:04,011 --> 00:02:08,211
Beep-haw! Beep-haw! Beep-haw!

7
00:02:08,211 --> 00:02:11,011
It's flying! Quick, don't let it get away!

8
00:02:11,011 --> 00:02:13,011
Let's get up ahead of it and block its course!

9
00:02:17,711 --> 00:02:19,711
I guess we ran ashore or something.

10
00:02:19,711 --> 00:02:22,211
What is that sound?

11
00:02:39,811 --> 00:02:43,411
Full reverse right now! Turn 180 degrees!

12
00:02:45,311 --> 00:02:48,011
The Dashing Sea Train and the City of Water!

13
00:02:48,011 --> 00:02:49,011
Water 7!

14
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:54,711
What the hell is that?

15
00:02:54,711 --> 00:02:56,711
Turn the ship around now!

16
00:02:56,711 --> 00:02:57,711
Hooray!

17
00:02:57,711 --> 00:02:58,711
Grr!

18
00:02:58,711 --> 00:02:59,711
Grr!

19
00:02:59,711 --> 00:03:00,711
Grr!

20
00:03:00,711 --> 00:03:01,711
Grr!

21
00:03:01,711 --> 00:03:02,711
Grr!

22
00:03:02,711 --> 00:03:03,711
Grr!

23
00:03:07,711 --> 00:03:08,711
Grr!

24
00:03:08,711 --> 00:03:09,711
Grr!

25
00:03:09,711 --> 00:03:16,711
Grr!

26
00:03:20,711 --> 00:03:21,711
Grr!

27
00:03:21,711 --> 00:03:22,711
Grr!

28
00:03:22,711 --> 00:03:23,711
Grr!

29
00:03:23,711 --> 00:03:24,711
Whoa! That was gross!

30
00:03:26,711 --> 00:03:28,711
The Hulk of Metal is trying to kill us!

31
00:03:28,711 --> 00:03:30,711
Is it a ship?

32
00:03:30,711 --> 00:03:34,711
No way! Something that big and heavy shouldn't even be able to fly!

33
00:03:37,711 --> 00:03:40,711
Hey! What are you doing? Get out of the way!

34
00:03:48,711 --> 00:03:50,711
Oh no! Froggy!

35
00:03:58,711 --> 00:04:18,711
It looked like it was spitting out smoke!

36
00:04:28,711 --> 00:04:30,711
Pirates?

37
00:04:30,711 --> 00:04:32,711
Granny! Granny! Look, we have pirates!

38
00:04:32,711 --> 00:04:34,711
What? Is that true, Timmy?

39
00:04:34,711 --> 00:04:36,711
Okey-dokey, then in that case,

40
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:40,711
better bring Granny the transponder snail!

41
00:04:40,711 --> 00:04:44,711
It's gonna be a big pain if they call for help when the Marines show up.

42
00:04:44,711 --> 00:04:46,711
What should we do?

43
00:04:46,711 --> 00:04:48,711
Here it is, Granny!

44
00:04:48,711 --> 00:04:50,711
Um, hello?

45
00:04:50,711 --> 00:04:52,711
Who is this?

46
00:04:52,711 --> 00:04:55,711
Sorry, you got the wrong number.

47
00:04:55,711 --> 00:04:57,711
She's totally drunk!

48
00:04:58,711 --> 00:05:03,711
Oh, bye, huh?

49
00:05:03,711 --> 00:05:06,711
That stuff goes good with booze!

50
00:05:06,711 --> 00:05:09,711
Mmm! Yummy!

51
00:05:09,711 --> 00:05:10,711
My name's Chimney!

52
00:05:10,711 --> 00:05:12,711
This is our kitty cat Gombe!

53
00:05:12,711 --> 00:05:14,711
And that's Granny Kokoro!

54
00:05:14,711 --> 00:05:17,711
You fellas wouldn't happen to be train robbers, would ya?

55
00:05:18,711 --> 00:05:21,711
My name's Luffy, and I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

56
00:05:21,711 --> 00:05:22,711
Really?

57
00:05:22,711 --> 00:05:23,711
Yep!

58
00:05:24,711 --> 00:05:26,711
I like you, you're funny!

59
00:05:26,711 --> 00:05:29,711
By the way, Chimney, that thing's a steamboat, right?

60
00:05:29,711 --> 00:05:30,711
Seems awfully long to me.

61
00:05:30,711 --> 00:05:32,711
Can't imagine it getting very far.

62
00:05:32,711 --> 00:05:37,711
You've probably never seen anything like this, seeing as it's the only one in the world!

63
00:05:37,711 --> 00:05:41,711
It's not a steamboat, it's a sea train called the Puffing Tom!

64
00:05:41,711 --> 00:05:42,711
How does it work?

65
00:05:42,711 --> 00:05:46,711
It ordered a steam engine to turn its paddle wheels and run on a railway!

66
00:05:50,711 --> 00:05:51,711
Railway?

67
00:05:51,711 --> 00:05:52,711
Uh-huh!

68
00:05:52,711 --> 00:05:54,711
If you look close, you can see the tracks right below the waves!

69
00:05:54,711 --> 00:05:58,711
The train goes the same route every day, taking people from one island to the next!

70
00:05:58,711 --> 00:06:01,711
It carries ships and packages and other stuff, too!

71
00:06:01,711 --> 00:06:02,711
Oh, wow!

72
00:06:02,711 --> 00:06:03,711
Funny we didn't notice it before!

73
00:06:03,711 --> 00:06:05,711
No kidding, we ran right into it!

74
00:06:05,711 --> 00:06:07,711
You should be more careful!

75
00:06:07,711 --> 00:06:08,711
Didn't you see the signal?

76
00:06:08,711 --> 00:06:10,711
There's a bell ringing and everything!

77
00:06:10,711 --> 00:06:11,711
Is that what that thing is for?

78
00:06:11,711 --> 00:06:13,711
I thought it was just here to welcome us!

79
00:06:13,711 --> 00:06:15,711
How are we supposed to know?

80
00:06:15,711 --> 00:06:18,711
And if we couldn't figure it out, then that frog sure wouldn't get it, would he?

81
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:20,711
It was awful rude of you to hit him like that!

82
00:06:20,711 --> 00:06:22,711
We were gonna catch him and cook him, you know!

83
00:06:22,711 --> 00:06:23,711
Oh!

84
00:06:23,711 --> 00:06:24,711
You saw the frog?

85
00:06:24,711 --> 00:06:25,711
That's Yokozuna!

86
00:06:25,711 --> 00:06:27,711
He sure was an awesome swimmer!

87
00:06:27,711 --> 00:06:30,711
Either way, I wouldn't worry about him, he's pretty tough!

88
00:06:30,711 --> 00:06:33,711
In fact, that wasn't the first time he's challenged the train and lost!

89
00:06:33,711 --> 00:06:35,711
He's really kind of a pain!

90
00:06:35,711 --> 00:06:38,711
If you wanna see him again, just hang around here, I'm sure he'll pop up!

91
00:06:38,711 --> 00:06:40,711
That's why he didn't run!

92
00:06:40,711 --> 00:06:44,711
Wow, I thought that frog was stupid, but it turns out he was just being super manly!

93
00:06:44,711 --> 00:06:45,711
Easy for you to say!

94
00:06:45,711 --> 00:06:47,711
You don't have to put up with him all the time!

95
00:06:47,711 --> 00:06:50,711
I can't even count how many times he's broken the rail cord!

96
00:06:50,711 --> 00:06:54,711
And just imagine what it's like for the passengers when he slams into the train!

97
00:06:54,711 --> 00:06:56,711
That's pretty crazy!

98
00:06:56,711 --> 00:07:00,711
Okay, since that frog's a fighter like me, I'm not gonna eat him after all!

99
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,711
Who would wanna eat that gross thing in the first place?

100
00:07:02,711 --> 00:07:06,711
Anyways, after this, where are you folks headed off to?

101
00:07:06,711 --> 00:07:09,711
The sea train runs to all sorts of places!

102
00:07:11,711 --> 00:07:14,711
There's the town of the Spring Queen, St. Poplar!

103
00:07:14,711 --> 00:07:19,711
There's the gourmet town Pucci, or the carnival town San Faldo!

104
00:07:19,711 --> 00:07:21,711
They're all fun places to go!

105
00:07:21,711 --> 00:07:25,711
And if you happen to work for the government, you can take a special train that's even fancier

106
00:07:25,711 --> 00:07:27,711
than the puffing tom!

107
00:07:27,711 --> 00:07:29,711
The gourmet town Pucci?

108
00:07:29,711 --> 00:07:33,711
Oh, that's the place those people we met on the island were talking about!

109
00:07:33,711 --> 00:07:35,711
Hey, you're right!

110
00:07:39,711 --> 00:07:41,711
Good, then that's the place we're gonna go!

111
00:07:41,711 --> 00:07:42,711
Give it up!

112
00:07:42,711 --> 00:07:46,711
Thanks, but there's no reason for us to take the train when we have our own ship.

113
00:07:46,711 --> 00:07:47,711
We'll just follow the log.

114
00:07:47,711 --> 00:07:49,711
Oh? Where's it pointing to?

115
00:07:49,711 --> 00:07:51,711
Should be someplace east of here.

116
00:07:51,711 --> 00:07:52,711
I see.

117
00:07:52,711 --> 00:07:55,711
Well, in that case, it's Water 7 for sure.

118
00:07:55,711 --> 00:08:00,711
The train you saw on the way here just came from Blue Station on that island.

119
00:08:00,711 --> 00:08:02,711
They call it the City of Water.

120
00:08:02,711 --> 00:08:03,711
I think you'll like it.

121
00:08:03,711 --> 00:08:04,711
Water 7, huh?

122
00:08:04,711 --> 00:08:06,711
They got great shipyards.

123
00:08:06,711 --> 00:08:08,711
You might say that's their claim to fame.

124
00:08:08,711 --> 00:08:10,711
When it comes to boats, they're first class.

125
00:08:10,711 --> 00:08:15,711
They're always coming up with some fancy new technology to build boats for the world government.

126
00:08:15,711 --> 00:08:16,711
Whoa!

127
00:08:16,711 --> 00:08:19,711
Then they must have some awesome shipwrights too!

128
00:08:19,711 --> 00:08:20,711
Some?

129
00:08:20,711 --> 00:08:22,711
More like damn near all of them.

130
00:08:22,711 --> 00:08:25,711
The city's like a regular shipwrights convention!

131
00:08:25,711 --> 00:08:26,711
You hear that?

132
00:08:26,711 --> 00:08:27,711
Yeah!

133
00:08:27,711 --> 00:08:29,711
All right then, it's settled!

134
00:08:29,711 --> 00:08:32,711
We're gonna find the best shipwright in Water 7 and get him to join our crew!

135
00:08:32,711 --> 00:08:34,711
Oh, is that so?

136
00:08:34,711 --> 00:08:36,711
In that case, hold on a sec.

137
00:08:36,711 --> 00:08:37,711
Oopsy-daisy!

138
00:08:37,711 --> 00:08:38,711
You can do it!

139
00:08:38,711 --> 00:08:40,711
Where's she going?

140
00:08:40,711 --> 00:08:41,711
Don't know.

141
00:08:41,711 --> 00:08:43,711
I got a present for you.

142
00:08:43,711 --> 00:08:46,711
This is a little map of the city and a reference letter.

143
00:08:46,711 --> 00:08:51,711
Just give this to a fellow named Iceberg and I promise he'll fix your ship up good.

144
00:08:51,711 --> 00:08:53,711
Water 7's a pretty confusing place.

145
00:08:53,711 --> 00:08:55,711
Be sure not to get lost.

146
00:08:55,711 --> 00:08:57,711
You have a big heart, don't you?

147
00:08:57,711 --> 00:08:59,711
We really owe you one!

148
00:09:03,711 --> 00:09:06,711
We'll be heading back to Water 7 soon, so maybe we'll see you there!

149
00:09:06,711 --> 00:09:08,711
Sounds like a plan to me!

150
00:09:08,711 --> 00:09:12,711
And if you like, I can even give you folks a tour of all my favorite drinking holes!

151
00:09:13,711 --> 00:09:14,711
Sounds good!

152
00:09:14,711 --> 00:09:16,711
We'll try to keep a lookout for you!

153
00:09:16,711 --> 00:09:21,711
It'll take about a week for the log to lock onto the next island, so you'll have plenty of time to do some sightseeing!

154
00:09:22,711 --> 00:09:23,711
Great!

155
00:09:23,711 --> 00:09:24,711
Should be fun!

156
00:09:25,711 --> 00:09:26,711
Okay!

157
00:09:26,711 --> 00:09:27,711
Everyone ready?

158
00:09:27,711 --> 00:09:29,711
Time to set sail!

159
00:09:29,711 --> 00:09:30,711
Yeah!

160
00:09:30,711 --> 00:09:32,711
Thanks again for the map and reference letter!

161
00:09:32,711 --> 00:09:34,711
I sure am glad we ran into you on the way!

162
00:09:38,711 --> 00:09:40,711
Have a safe trip!

163
00:09:40,711 --> 00:09:41,711
Yeah!

164
00:09:41,711 --> 00:09:43,711
Better keep an eye out for all those government types down there!

165
00:09:43,711 --> 00:09:44,711
Yahoo!

166
00:09:44,711 --> 00:09:45,711
Let's go!

167
00:09:45,711 --> 00:09:46,711
City of Meat, here we come!

168
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:47,711
Did you forget where we're going already?

169
00:09:48,711 --> 00:09:49,711
What a nice wind!

170
00:09:49,711 --> 00:09:51,711
Let's go!

171
00:09:51,711 --> 00:09:53,711
City of Meat, here we come!

172
00:09:53,711 --> 00:09:56,711
Did you forget where we're going already?

173
00:10:14,711 --> 00:10:16,711
What a nice wind.

174
00:10:16,711 --> 00:10:19,711
We might make it out to Water 7 even faster than I thought.

175
00:10:19,711 --> 00:10:21,711
I'll be happy either way.

176
00:10:21,711 --> 00:10:22,711
Don't worry about finding a shipwright.

177
00:10:22,711 --> 00:10:24,711
I got it all under control.

178
00:10:24,711 --> 00:10:26,711
I'll get the hottest girl in town guaranteed.

179
00:10:26,711 --> 00:10:28,711
Who do I care if the shipwright's hot?

180
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:30,711
I want a huge, manly dude, like even bigger than a bear!

181
00:10:30,711 --> 00:10:32,711
Sixteen feet tall!

182
00:10:32,711 --> 00:10:34,711
A guy that size couldn't even fit on the ship,

183
00:10:34,711 --> 00:10:36,711
and who knows how much food he would have to eat!

184
00:10:36,711 --> 00:10:38,711
All that matters is that he's good at his job.

185
00:10:38,711 --> 00:10:40,711
If you ask me, the real problem's gonna be

186
00:10:40,711 --> 00:10:42,711
finding someone crazy enough to go sailing

187
00:10:42,711 --> 00:10:44,711
with a bunch of pirates.

188
00:10:44,711 --> 00:10:45,711
Size doesn't matter.

189
00:10:45,711 --> 00:10:47,711
I'm just glad we're gonna make a new friend.

190
00:10:47,711 --> 00:10:49,711
We're lucky we ran into that train station on the way.

191
00:10:49,711 --> 00:10:51,711
This map should be a big help.

192
00:10:51,711 --> 00:10:53,711
All we have to do is follow Kokoro's directions

193
00:10:53,711 --> 00:10:55,711
to that iceberg guy and we're set.

194
00:10:55,711 --> 00:10:57,711
I see.

195
00:10:57,711 --> 00:10:59,711
Stupid drunk!

196
00:10:59,711 --> 00:11:01,711
Whoa, looks like Luffy's art.

197
00:11:01,711 --> 00:11:03,711
Okay, let's try to find a shipwright

198
00:11:03,711 --> 00:11:05,711
that looks something like this!

199
00:11:05,711 --> 00:11:07,711
If I saw a guy like that, I'd run!

200
00:11:07,711 --> 00:11:09,711
I wouldn't just run, I'd jump into the sea

201
00:11:09,711 --> 00:11:11,711
to get away from that freak.

202
00:11:11,711 --> 00:11:13,711
He might be part octopus, so even that might not save me.

203
00:11:13,711 --> 00:11:15,711
Don't you have anything better to talk about?

204
00:11:15,711 --> 00:11:17,711
Okay, everybody, since we're gonna be

205
00:11:17,711 --> 00:11:19,711
at Water 7 for a whole week,

206
00:11:19,711 --> 00:11:21,711
let me give you your allowance!

207
00:11:21,711 --> 00:11:23,711
Oh, me first! Me first!

208
00:11:23,711 --> 00:11:25,711
Gimme, gimme!

209
00:11:25,711 --> 00:11:27,711
Please, everyone!

210
00:11:27,711 --> 00:11:31,711
Allowance! Allowance! Allowance! Allowance!

211
00:11:41,711 --> 00:11:43,711
Why are you hugging the ship, Usopp?

212
00:11:43,711 --> 00:11:45,711
I know all these tent plates may not look like much to you,

213
00:11:45,711 --> 00:11:47,711
but they bring back a lot of fond memories for me.

214
00:11:47,711 --> 00:11:49,711
I almost hate to see them go,

215
00:11:49,711 --> 00:11:51,711
but it'll all be worth it if the Mary can finally

216
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:53,711
get the repairs she needs!

217
00:11:53,711 --> 00:11:54,711
I feel the same way.

218
00:11:54,711 --> 00:11:56,711
I'm proud of her battle scars like anyone else,

219
00:11:56,711 --> 00:11:57,711
but she's taken a real beating

220
00:11:57,711 --> 00:11:59,711
since we've entered the Grand Line.

221
00:11:59,711 --> 00:12:01,711
The deck squeaks and we've got leaks

222
00:12:01,711 --> 00:12:03,711
popping up everywhere.

223
00:12:03,711 --> 00:12:04,711
Nobody wants to admit it,

224
00:12:04,711 --> 00:12:05,711
but if we don't fix this soon,

225
00:12:05,711 --> 00:12:06,711
we're as good as sunk.

226
00:12:06,711 --> 00:12:08,711
Yeah, but even if we can't get a shipwright

227
00:12:08,711 --> 00:12:10,711
for the crew, we still have plenty of money!

228
00:12:10,711 --> 00:12:12,711
We can do more than just fix her!

229
00:12:12,711 --> 00:12:13,711
We can power her up, too!

230
00:12:13,711 --> 00:12:15,711
Ooh! Then let's get more cannons!

231
00:12:15,711 --> 00:12:17,711
Yeah! And a big statue!

232
00:12:17,711 --> 00:12:19,711
Hm. Hey, I think we're there!

233
00:12:19,711 --> 00:12:23,711
Huh?

234
00:12:23,711 --> 00:12:27,711
He's right! I can see Water 7!

235
00:12:27,711 --> 00:12:29,711
All right, men! Time to roll!

236
00:12:29,711 --> 00:12:30,711
The wind's enough.

237
00:12:30,711 --> 00:12:33,711
Don't wear us out before we even get there.

238
00:12:43,711 --> 00:12:45,711
Lovely.

239
00:12:45,711 --> 00:12:47,711
Wow!

240
00:12:47,711 --> 00:12:57,711
Nobody told me it was gonna be this cool!

241
00:12:57,711 --> 00:12:59,711
Whoa!

242
00:12:59,711 --> 00:13:01,711
Check that thing out!

243
00:13:01,711 --> 00:13:06,711
I didn't know they made fountains that big!

244
00:13:06,711 --> 00:13:08,711
Oh! That's nuts!

245
00:13:08,711 --> 00:13:10,711
I've never seen anything like it!

246
00:13:10,711 --> 00:13:12,711
And I thought the sea train was a big deal.

247
00:13:12,711 --> 00:13:15,711
Oh, wow! That's a lot of water!

248
00:13:15,711 --> 00:13:18,711
Do you think it all comes from the ocean?

249
00:13:18,711 --> 00:13:20,711
That's what it seems like.

250
00:13:20,711 --> 00:13:21,711
Then it pours out of the fountain,

251
00:13:21,711 --> 00:13:22,711
goes through the canals,

252
00:13:22,711 --> 00:13:24,711
and falls back into the sea.

253
00:13:28,711 --> 00:13:29,711
Hey! Once we get there,

254
00:13:29,711 --> 00:13:31,711
let's have a race on those water slides!

255
00:13:31,711 --> 00:13:32,711
Water slides?

256
00:13:32,711 --> 00:13:40,711
I think I'll pass!

257
00:13:40,711 --> 00:13:42,711
Even if that was a water slide,

258
00:13:42,711 --> 00:13:43,711
you still can't swim.

259
00:13:43,711 --> 00:13:44,711
Oh, good point.

260
00:13:44,711 --> 00:13:45,711
By the way,

261
00:13:45,711 --> 00:13:47,711
do you have any idea what those numbers mean?

262
00:13:47,711 --> 00:13:49,711
Hmm, good question.

263
00:13:49,711 --> 00:13:51,711
They look like walls,

264
00:13:51,711 --> 00:13:53,711
but they could be some kind of gate.

265
00:13:53,711 --> 00:13:54,711
Duh, those are special entrances

266
00:13:54,711 --> 00:13:56,711
where all the 16-foot shipwrights go in.

267
